  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nOverall, weather will be mild and dry through the upcoming work\nweek. The main concern will be gusty winds along the Rocky\nMountain Front Thursday through Friday night.\n\nAn upper-level ridge develops over the region today and remains in\nplace through Tuesday, resulting in dry and mild weather. The\nupper-level ridge weakens and collapses over Tuesday night as a\nweak cut-off upper-level low tracks east across Utah and Colorado.\nNo major weather shifts are expected from this low, although there\nwill be cooler weather on Wednesday compared to Tuesday. Weak \nupper-level ridging develops over Wednesday night, but quickly \nbegins deteriorating and shifting eastward over Thursday. \nFollowing the movement of the ridge, an upper-level trough begins \nmoving eastward into the region and bringing southwesterly flow \naloft. As a result, winds pick up along the Rocky Mountain Front \nbut gusts are currently expected to remain under 40 mph. As the \ntrough continues its eastward movement, winds will increase and \nshift westerly over Thursday night. The upper-level pressure \ngradient compresses over Friday and remains compressed through \nFriday night, resulting in increased winds along the Rocky \nMountain Front and central MT with gusts up to 60 mph. There is \nthe potential for showers Thursday through Friday, but showers \ncurrently look inclined to remain west of the divide.\n\nLooking towards Saturday and beyond, a new upper-level ridge\nbegins to establish itself. Likely leading to a continuation of\nmild and dry weather. Winds decrease over Saturday, but areas of\nbreezy winds will remain possible. -ESH\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\n...Winds exceeding 60 mph Thursday night through Friday night...\n\nThursday Night: 25% chance for gusts to exceed 60 mph for the \nRocky Mountain Front.\n\nFriday: 30% chance for gusts to exceed 60 mph for the Rocky \nMountain Front.\n\nFriday Night: 55% chance for gusts to exceed 60 mph for the Rocky\nMountain Front. 20% chance for gusts to exceed 60 mph along the\neastern slopes of the Little Belts. -ESH",
